            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan Pascullo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This dressing is a nice alternative to the raspberry vinaigrettes I have had in the past. Tastes extremely fresh, slightly sweet and orangy with a little kick from the Cayenne pepper. It was a perfect topping for the salad greens I served with a Chicken Cordon Bleu dish and balsamic glazed asparagus. My husband asked to have this dressing on a regular basis... quite a compliment! Thanks for sharing!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cat Hill"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really liked it. The DH said he couldn't really taste it but I served it over organic spinach which was pretty strong flavored. I did forget the orange zest and I did find the dressing to be a little too runny. I figured since I was trying something new on the guys it had better look closer to store bought so I got out my smallest saucepan and reduced the dressing. Differently will be using this recipe again!",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-23T05:44:25.180Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TerriLeeAnn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A fabulous dressing for any summer salad, especially one with fruit! It's the perfect blend of sweet &amp; tangy. I made it for a spinach salad with berries, mandarin oranges &amp; pecans. I left out the cayenne pepper and used powdered ginger instead. I used pear infused white balsamic vinegar. It got rave reviews. Fresh vinaigrette is always the best - I'll definitely make it again!",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-22T02:46:44.200Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Beatriz Manrique"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I did some changes, i used wine vinegar did not have white, a chopped garlic, 2 tablespoon of white sugar and 1 spoon of a dijon mustard ...love it, sweeter but not to much, the garlic did his part....perfect balance",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-22T16:47:19.250Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Volleyballmom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great dressing for orange lovers. It is runny like others mentioned but I didn't mind. Served it on romaine with mandarin wedges, walnuts and cranraisins. I totally forgot to use the orange peel. I don't think it was missed. Parsley was a nice touch, added to the 'fresh' taste. thx LaurasFaves.",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-27T05:29:32.373Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MichelleDevon Michy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It's a slightly runny dressing, but the flavor is amazing. It was absolutely perfect for my citrus marinated chicken and greens salad. Has just enough sweetness with just enough kick. I did not have white-wine vinegar, so I used red-wine vinegar instead, but it turned out beautifully anyway. Just don't use full white vinegar--too much tang that way. Really excellent and pretty simple recipe. I used organic honey, with no ingredients other than 'honey' in it. I highly recommend it for a slightly sweet dressing for any bitter greens or chicken salads.",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-09T11:49:35.623Z"
          },
          {
